No database.

POST /api/assessment/evaluate

must use the server-side assessment record.

The client must NOT submit:
correctOptionIndex

and have the server trust it.

Client-submitted answer keys MUST be ignored/rejected.

This is mandatory.

==================================================
PHASE 2 — INTERVIEW SESSION INTEGRITY
==================================================

Audit:

/api/interview/start
/api/interview/respond
/api/interview/complete

The server should maintain enough session state to prevent the client from rewriting its own interview history.

Do not trust the browser to invent:

- previous understanding
- misconceptions
- previous questions
- next concept
- interview score
- completion state

Use a bounded server-side session store.

No database required.

At minimum store:

sessionId
topic
target concepts
turn history
current question
current concept
status
max turns
evidence

When `/respond` arrives:
- verify session exists
- append the real learner response
- evaluate it
- generate the next question
- persist the new state

When `/complete` arrives:
- use server session history
- ignore forged client history
- generate summary from trusted history

This is mandatory.

